    2. Decide a connection graph: choose 2-4 edges, each either horizontal or vertical, with gap length 1-5.
    3. Place connected marker centers first ensuring shared row/column per edge, non-overlapping 3x3 bboxes, gap paths clear of other markers, and centers >=1 from edges.
    4. Optionally place 0-1 unconnected markers (unique row AND column) with same spacing constraints.
    5. Build output by drawing all markers (RED plus arms) and filling gaps with BLUE.
